From 0129e0596da21e0ca1c8def589af8f126ab7584f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Svitlana Drozd <svitlana_drozd@epam.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:30:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] common: utils: fswatcher: fix compilation with GCC 15

GCC 15 enforces stricter header hygiene and no longer transitively
includes standard library headers, causing compilation errors due to a
missing `#include <algorithm>` for `std::find` and `std::find_if` in `fswatcher.cpp`.

Explicitly include `<algorithm>` to resolve build failures under the
Wrynose release toolchain.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Svitlana Drozd <svitlana_drozd@epam.com>
---
 src/common/utils/fswatcher.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/common/utils/fswatcher.cpp b/src/common/utils/fswatcher.cpp
index 55c93402..e7c671d9 100644
--- a/src/common/utils/fswatcher.cpp
+++ b/src/common/utils/fswatcher.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <sys/inotify.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <vector>
+#include <algorithm>
 
 #include <Poco/UUID.h>
 #include <Poco/UUIDGenerator.h>
